# Auto Commit & Push to Main

After completing any code changes in this project:

1. Run `git status` and include all relevant changed files.
2. Commit with a clear, concise message focused on why.
3. Push to `origin/main` immediately without waiting for the user to ask.
4. Never commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, credentials).

Skip only when the user explicitly says not to commit, or when there are no changes.
